    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Okay, I see your point about the directionality. But looking at the technical claims in that 2018 patent again, they mention \"spatial resolution of tactile inputs across an actuator grid\" and \"varying response to localized pressure changes.\" \n\nIf the examiner compares that \"spatial resolution\" and \"varying response\" to our client's \"multi-directional pressure gradient response,\" aren't they going to say it's effectively the same thing? I'm worried our argument about directionality is a bit thin. Are there any other specific technical components in the 2018 patent that we can point to as being fundamentally different from our client's setup to make this case stronger?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
